-- title:
--   Triangle inequality for a sum of five terms
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ be a seminormed additive group and let $a, b, c, d, e \in E$. Then the norm of the five-fold sum is bounded by the sum of the norms:
--
--   $$\|a + b + c + d + e\| \;\le\; \|a\| + \|b\| + \|c\| + \|d\| + \|e\|.$$
--
--   This is the five-term iteration of the triangle inequality. In the PNT+ zeta-bounds development, error terms naturally split into five (or six) pieces --- for example the Euler--Maclaurin representation of $\zeta$ contributes a finite sum, two boundary terms, and integral remainders --- and this lemma bounds the total in a single step instead of a chain of binary triangle inequalities.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/AlexKontorovich/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd/blob/f55e85551ac10e96d98262a354cfcaac2825f2da/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd/ZetaBounds.lean#L1201-L1204

